# Development Journal

## Task 1 - Planning the project

### What I worked on

I started by reviewing the project requirements and deciding on a simple application to build. I chose to create a Quote Generator.

The goal of the application was to allow users to view inspirational or motivational quotes and generate a new quote by clicking a button.

### Decisions I made

I decided to keep the scope of the project small and focus on the main functionality instead of adding unnecessary features.

The core features I identified were:

Displaying a quote
Generating a new quote when the user clicks a button
Creating a simple and easy-to-use interface

I chose HTML, CSS, and JavaScript because they were sufficient for building the core functionality.



## Task 2 – Building the interface

### What I worked on

I created the basic structure and design of the Quote Generator.

### Decisions I made

I chose a simple layout so that users could immediately understand how to interact with the application.
I decided to use a clean and minimal design so that the quote would remain the main focus of the application.


## Task 3 – Adjusting accesibility

### What I worked on

Removing the toggle. Not just hiding it — pulling out the dark theme styles and the switching logic so there's no dead code or half-supported state left behind.
Changed the primary color to a Purple that actually works. Purple can get muddy or low-contrast fast, especially in mid-tones used for buttons or links. I picked a shade knowing it would need to hold a 4.5:1 ratio against the light background, not just look right at first glance.

### Challenges

I discovered that users could submit an empty habit.

### How I solved them

I added validation to prevent empty values from being added to the habit list.


## Task 4 – Testing and documentation

### What I worked on

I tested the main features of the application and fixed issues that appeared during testing.

I also created the README.md and journal.md files.

### Final result

The application allows users to generate, share, listen and favorite a quote
